{
 "_": "One taxonomy for every fashion shop, as a storefront lays it out: departments, then categories, then their sub-menus. A product sits under a node when it meets the node's rule: `match` names product fields (dot paths) and the values that count; `garment` names words that one of its garments carries. A category with `from` takes its sub-menus from that field's values (a shop's own collections). scripts/catalog.mjs writes each product's places (`catalog`) into the product data; lib/catalog.js builds the menu from them, for the app and for Phiora (GET /shop/catalog). A node with no product is not shown.",
 "departments": [
  { "id": "women", "label": "Women", "match": { "specs.gender": ["Womenswear", "Unisex", "Genderless"] } },
  { "id": "men", "label": "Men", "match": { "specs.gender": ["Menswear", "Unisex", "Genderless"] } }
 ],
 "categories": [
